# exporter.env - the exporter's NON-secret connection settings (compose env_file).
#
# The password is not here: DATA_SOURCE_PASS_FILE names a file that compose mounts
# from the db_monitor_password secret, so `docker inspect` shows a path and never a
# value. The role is app_monitor: member of pg_monitor, not superuser, connection
# limit and timeouts set in bootstrap/roles.sql.
#
# TLS: the server only accepts TCP over TLS (conf/pg_hba.conf). sslmode=verify-full
# checks the chain AND the host name: bootstrap/tls-init.sh signs the development
# certificate for DNS:db, and the exporter trusts that certificate itself
# (sslrootcert=/tls/server.crt, from the read-only dbtls volume). A real deployment
# mounts its own CA bundle at that path instead; never weaken the mode.
#
# UNVERIFIED against v0.21.1 in a container: these three variable names are the
# documented non-deprecated way to pass a connection without a password in the URI;
# the release notes say deprecated variables go in v0.22.0. db-scrape-test.sh
# (pg_up == 1) is the proof after every bump.
DATA_SOURCE_URI=db:5432/app?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/tls/server.crt
DATA_SOURCE_USER=app_monitor
DATA_SOURCE_PASS_FILE=/run/secrets/db_monitor_password
